# GitHub
Who wrote Solid, its issues, and anyone on GitHub by their login.
Every thing it shows is in GitHub.api.spell, as `spell place ingest` wrote it;  each type below adds to its type there,
with `<spell-more-of>`, so looking again at the server never touches a line of this.
A page in a browser holds no key:  it asks as anyone does, 60 times an hour, so it checks for changes every half hour.

<spell-thing "github page">
	<spell>
		- its "login" is text
		- to create it:
			set its login to "ryansolid"
	</spell>
	<property "person" description="Whoever has that login:  GitHub finds them by it, with no list of everyone">the user whose id is its login</property>

	<draw>
		<header size="large">Solid, on GitHub</header>
		<form value={it}>
			<field label="Anyone on GitHub, by their login">
				<input name="login" icon="search" placeholder="ryansolid" />
			</field>
		</form>
		draw its profile
		<header size="medium">Who wrote it</header>
		<for every contributor as="cards" columns="5" doubling loading="Asking GitHub" failed="GitHub can't be reached just now." />
		<header size="medium">Its issues</header>
		<for every issue as="cards" columns="2" doubling loading="Asking GitHub" failed="GitHub can't be reached just now." />
		<text size="small">
			From <link link="https://docs.github.com/en/rest">GitHub's REST API</link>, asked for as you look.
		</text>
	</draw>

	<draw "profile">
		<if its person>
			draw its person's card
		</if>
		while waiting:
			<loader visible inline text>Asking GitHub</loader>
		if that fails:
			<text>Nobody on GitHub has that login.</text>
	</draw>
</spell-thing>


# Someone on GitHub
Their picture, their name, and what they've made public.

<spell-more-of "user">
	<draw "card">
		<ui-card>
			<image src={its avatar url} alt="" />
			<content>
				<header>{its name}</header>
				<meta>{its login}</meta>
			</content>
			<extra>{its public repos} public repositories · {its followers} followers</extra>
		</ui-card>
	</draw>
</spell-more-of>

<spell-more-of "contributor">
	<draw>
		<ui-card>
			<image src={its avatar url} alt="" />
			<content>
				<header>{its login}</header>
				<meta>{its contributions} contributions</meta>
			</content>
		</ui-card>
	</draw>
</spell-more-of>


# An issue
Its number, its title, whose it is, and how much it's been talked about.

<spell-more-of "issue">
	<draw>
		<ui-card>
			<content>
				<header>#{its number} {its title}</header>
				<meta>{its state} · {its user's login} · {its comments} comments</meta>
			</content>
		</ui-card>
	</draw>
</spell-more-of>
